    "description": "A graph database supplies a custom forward iterator over immutable node records. Its dereference, increment, and advancement operations intentionally remain implementation details so that only the iterator facade controls traversal, reference lifetime, and boundary behavior. A reusable iterator adapter library needs to invoke those core operations while implementing the standard iterator operations and allowing only the adapter's traversal hooks, not the complete private surface of the iterator, to be reached. Establish a named internal access gateway that the custom iterator alone authorizes, and let the adapter call through that gateway to perform dereference and movement. The adapter must not obtain direct access to the stored node pointer, the iterator's comparison internals, or unrelated state. The result must continue to compile with the standard facade and must prevent arbitrary user code from invoking the core hooks directly.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose how to give the iterator adapter compile-time access to the custom iterator's core hooks without exposing its storage or unrelated private operations.",
    "notes": "A named gateway forwards the iterator's core traversal hooks to the adapter without exposing storage; passkey is the near miss for gating the same hooks with a token."
  },
